export default {"id":"komplete-level-11","number":11,"title":"Komplete Kontrol in Live 12 Standard","skillBand":"Textbook","duration":"From the course textbook","summary":"— Insert, play, record","modules":[{"id":"komplete-m-11-1-2","code":"11.1","title":"— Insert, play, record","blurb":"— Insert, play, record","outcomes":[],"sources":[],"practiceFocus":[],"checkpoints":[],"lessons":[{"id":"komplete-kk-l11-1-1","title":"Insert, play, record","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"Module 11.1 — Insert, play, record","blocks":[{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>Outcomes:</strong> KK VST3 is on a Live MIDI track, plays, and records."},{"type":"table","headers":["Lesson","Title","Description","Authoring ID"],"rows":[["11.1.1","Why VST3 here","Official AU has <strong>no MIDI out</strong> for Scale/Arp. Windows has no AU. Academy lock = VST3 on both computers.","<code>kk-l11-1-1</code>"],["11.1.2","Insert","Live Browser → Plug-ins → VST3 → Komplete Kontrol.","<code>kk-l11-1-2</code>"],["11.1.3","First launch as plug-in","Databases should already exist (Gate A). If the Browser is empty, quit Live, launch KK stand-alone once, return.","<code>kk-l11-1-3</code>"],["11.1.4","MIDI to the track","Record-arm. Input = the notes port of the keyboard/controller, not the DAW-control port.","<code>kk-l11-1-4</code>"],["11.1.5","Transport is Live’s","KK Play/Tempo are grey. Use Live’s transport.","<code>kk-l11-1-5</code>"],["11.1.6","Record notes","Session or Arrangement — Live course owns the views; this course owns “the notes came from KK.”","<code>kk-l11-1-6</code>"],["11.1.7","Record Scale/Arp as MIDI","Official outgoing MIDI. After record, you can turn Scale/Arp off and still hear the clip.","<code>kk-l11-1-7</code>"],["11.1.8","Multiple instances","Official 1.8+ concept still documented: several KK plug-ins can exist. Switching focus on an NI keyboard is a hardware lesson (Level 13).","<code>kk-l11-1-8</code>"]],"caption":null},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>mustCover:</strong> VST3; notes port vs DAW port; grey transport; record Arp MIDI.   <strong>mustNotCover:</strong> AU-on-Windows; inventing instance-switch buttons for non-NI keyboards.   <strong>Sources:</strong> Setting up; Automation MIDI out notice; Live 12 ch. 23 / 33 as Live-side reference.   <strong>Practice:</strong> One VST3 instance, one recorded MIDI clip that used Scale.   <strong>Checkpoint:</strong> Clip plays with KK’s Scale switched off."}]}],"minutes":8}],"exercises":[]},{"id":"komplete-m-11-2-3","code":"11.2","title":"— Automate Scale and Arp from Live","blurb":"— Automate Scale and Arp from Live","outcomes":[],"sources":[],"practiceFocus":[],"checkpoints":[],"lessons":[{"id":"komplete-kk-l11-2-1","title":"Automate Scale and Arp from Live","blocks":[{"type":"step","title":"Module 11.2 — Automate Scale and Arp from Live","blocks":[{"type":"table","headers":["Lesson","Title","Description","Authoring ID"],"rows":[["11.2.1","What Live can automate","Official: loaded instrument parameters, Scale parameters, Arp parameters.","<code>kk-l11-2-1</code>"],["11.2.2","Record a knob","Arm automation in Live (Live course gesture) → turn a KK / hardware knob.","<code>kk-l11-2-2</code>"],["11.2.3","Perform IDs exist","Show the official ID table once so a broken host mapping can be checked. Students operate from Live’s chooser, not by typing IDs.","<code>kk-l11-2-3</code>"],["11.2.4","ID 000","Reserved for instance recognition / automatic focus follow. Do not map student music to it.","<code>kk-l11-2-4</code>"]],"caption":null},{"type":"prose","html":"<strong>mustCover:</strong> Scale/Arp/instrument can be automated; 000 is reserved.   <strong>mustNotCover:</strong> a Live automation textbook.   <strong>Sources:</strong> DAW Automation; Live 12 automation chapter (sister).   <strong>Practice:</strong> Automate Arp Rate or Scale Type across four bars.   <strong>Checkpoint:</strong> <strong>Gate I.</strong>"}]}],"minutes":8}],"exercises":[]}]};
